    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for bugwarden",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for bugwarden fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in bugwarden:\n\n- Update to 0.7.1:\n  * Adopt rmcp 3.9.0 for RUSTSEC-2026-0462: it caps unbounded\n    Streamable HTTP client response buffering (16 MiB / 64 KiB);\n    toml rides along to 1.2.1.\n  * Name the anonymous landing and the API key placement in\n    identity preflight failures refused with code 410, instead of\n    blaming the endpoint or the login.\n\n- Update to 0.7.0:\n  * Add a changed_since filter to bugs_quicksearch\n  * Keep Bugzilla's error text out of read and write tool results\n  * Scrub Bug ID custom fields from served bugs, bug history and\n    write responses, and assess their targets before a write\n  * Refuse self-dependency and self-duplicate writes, quicksearch\n    predicates over hidden fields, and all-digit or path-unsafe\n    bug field names before any request\n  * Judge create_bug as Bugzilla will file it, and drop BMO's\n    comment_count from served bugs\n  * Audit stdio calls abandoned mid-dispatch and upstream errors\n    with Bugzilla's code; bound OTLP batches by encoded size\n  * By design, an initialize asking for 2026-07-28 now negotiates\n    2025-11-25: that revision has no handshake and is served to\n    clients that skip initialize\n  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes\n    for the full list\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.1-packagehub-43",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
